# Falkensteinkirche (1626), back-layer prop: the small white church built
# into a cave of the Falkensteinwand. Gable front whitewashed w (i shade on
# the right, i plinth), a b/s oculus, two round-arched b windows, an arched
# l/O door with brass Y handles under a small shingle porch roof; the nave's
# side wall i and its shingle roof O/l recede right into the cave; a white
# ridge turret (Dachreiter) with an open d belfry, an o/O bell, an O/l
# shingle onion and a small d iron cross. The rock m (i lit faces, d cracks,
# d shadowed underside) wraps round the back and over the roof; the cave
# wall behind the church is d with m ledges; its open left side stays
# transparent. No text, no outline (back layer). Drawn by the pixel-artist
# with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
